      "writtenOn": "2019-11-13T16:57:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If droidstub doesn\u0027t implement SdkAware interface, the sdk module will just ignore it. As a consequence, it won\u0027t intercept the dependency to the original droidstub and redirect it to the filegroup in the sdk_snapshot.\n\nFor the test, you can have a test Android.bp like below:\n\nsdk_snapshot {\n    name: \"mysdk@10\",\n    stubs_sources: [\"mystub_mysdk@10\"],\n}\n\nfilegroup {\n    name: \"mystub_mysdk@10\",\n    srcs: [\"foo/bar/FooStub.java\"],\n}\n\ndroidstub {\n    name: \"mystub\",\n    srcs: [\"foo/bar/Foo.java\"],\n}\n\napex {\n    name: \"myapex\",\n    java_libraries: [\"myjavalib\"],\n    usds_sdks: [\"mysdk@10\"],\n}\n\njava_library {\n    name: \"myjavalib\",\n    srcs: [\":mystub\"],\n}\n\nAnd check that android_common_myapex variant of myjavalib uses foo/bar/FooStub.java as its sources, instead of foo/bar/Foo.java.",
